Program fidelity is now clear: trusted regeneration is byte-identical, and the generated implementation matched a direct reading of the prompt on all 24,521 tests. It intentionally disagrees with the trusted canonical on 48 cases; importantly, many are prompt-valid dates such as `01-31-2000`, because the canonical’s unparenthesized conditions reject days 30–31 across months. I’ll carry that implementation-versus-canonical discrepancy into the adequacy judgment rather than silently treating either implementation as the contract.

Next I’m compiling both K definitions from the trusted source tree in scratch and running the two entry claims separately as well as together.
