+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -uo pipefail
+
+OUT=/audit-output/evidence/07_evidence_manifest.log
+TMP=/tmp/audit-work/124-valid-date/07_evidence_manifest.raw
+
+{
+  printf '%s\n' 'COMMAND: sha256sum reviewer-authored evidence artifacts'
+  find /audit-output/evidence -maxdepth 1 -type f \
+    ! -name '07_evidence_manifest.log' \
+    -print0 |
+    sort -z |
+    xargs -0 sha256sum
+  printf 'EXIT_STATUS: %s\n' "$?"
+} >"$TMP" 2>&1
+
+cp "$TMP" "$OUT"
+sed -n '1,320p' "$OUT"

Completed all seven audit stages, including clean reconstruction, exhaustive rule inventory, and a fresh rejected false-result mutation. REVIEW.md ends with CONCERNS / LEGIT because the proof is sound and prompt-complete but the trusted canonical contradicts the prompt on material inputs.
